\label{defsubstitute}
An \emph{$n$-ary substitute} is a mapping denoted $\underline{\lambda} x_1, \ldots, x_n . s$ or $\underline{\lambda} \vec{x} . s$, with $s$ a term, such that:
\begin{equation}
\label{pbetaeq}
(\underline{\lambda} \vec{x} . s)(t_1, \ldots, t_n) = s[\vec{x} := \vec{t}] \, .
\end{equation}

